From: Antigravity Autonomous Agent <engineering@lenovo-d330-fix.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: do not advertise render-compressed (CCS) modifiers on Lenovo IdeaPad D330

The Lenovo IdeaPad D330-10IGL (82H0) has a natively portrait panel that
userspace scans out rotated 90 or 270 degrees. i915 rejects a
render-compressed (CCS) scanout framebuffer combined with such a rotation in
skl_plane_check_fb() ("RC support only with 0/180 degree rotation ..."), so
every atomic commit that installs a rotated, CCS-backed primary plane fails
with -EINVAL. On resume the compositor recreates its framebuffer this way and
the repeated failed commit leaves the display black.

The plane still advertises CCS for XRGB/ARGB8888 in
skl_plane_format_mod_supported(), so compositors keep choosing it. Stop
advertising CCS on this platform; userspace then falls back to a Y-tiled
surface, which does support 90/270 rotation, and the resume commit succeeds.

Note: this only removes the plane-level rejection. A separate DSI panel
power/sequencing issue on resume (LP_RX_TIMEOUT, panel stays dark with no
image) is tracked separately and is not addressed here.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity Autonomous Agent <engineering@lenovo-d330-fix.local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c
index 746e942..45334d2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c
@@ -3,6 +3,8 @@
  * Copyright © 2020 Intel Corporation
  */
 
+#include <linux/dmi.h>
+
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_blend.h>
 #include <drm/drm_damage_helper.h>
@@ -2532,6 +2534,17 @@ static bool skl_plane_format_mod_supported(struct drm_plane *_plane,
 {
 	struct intel_plane *plane = to_intel_plane(_plane);
 
+	/*
+	 * Lenovo IdeaPad D330-10IGL: a CCS (render-compressed) framebuffer
+	 * cannot be scanned out with 90/270 rotation (skl_plane_check_fb
+	 * rejects it), so KWin's portrait output fails every atomic commit
+	 * after resume. Keep CCS out of this plane's IN_FORMATS so the
+	 * compositor picks a Y-tiled surface instead.
+	 */
+	if (dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "82H0") &&
+	    intel_fb_is_ccs_modifier(modifier))
+		return false;
+
 	if (!intel_fb_plane_supports_modifier(plane, modifier))
 		return false;
 
